    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d136">

                <pb facs="0233" n="153" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg153"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A3/1854: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-12-16T20:00:00+00:00">December 16,
                            1936—8 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 16—4:17 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>618. My 617, December 16, 6 p.m.<anchor n="40" xml:id="d136-f1"/> Foreign Office
                    states this afternoon Japanese Ambassador orally informed them that Japanese
                    Government is giving favorable consideration to the two proposals in question;
                    (1), as regards “C” class cruisers, (2), Japanese Government to escalate to
                    retain submarines.</p>
                <pb facs="0234" n="154" xml:id="pg154"/>
                <p>Yoshida explained this really meant complete acceptance but before formal
                    Japanese reply can be made it must be passed by Cabinet.</p>
                <p>Craigie says First Lord<anchor n="41" xml:id="d136-f2"/> will make statement in
                    Parliament tomorrow in this connection stating in substance that exchange of
                    views has taken place with United States and Japan. United States has replied if
                    Britain has recourse to escalator clause they have no objection and British
                    Government has reason to believe Japanese Government’s reply will be
                    favorable.</p>
                <p>Yoshida has agreed to above.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bingham</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
